# Professional structure

Keep this codebase tidy. Prefer moving files and extracting constants over dumping logic into components.

**Names:** `Mikeverse` = website and company. `Smile with Mike` = Instagram comedy page only. `Mike` = the character on all products.

## Folders

| Put here | What belongs |
|---|---|
| `src/config/` | Brand, routes, nav, env-backed settings |
| `src/content/` | Copy, FAQ, products, portfolio, JSON |
| `src/lib/` | Email, URL helpers, non-UI utilities |
| `src/components/` | UI only (chatbot, common, layout, sections) |
| `src/pages/` | Route screens |
| `src/app/` | Router |

## Code

- No unused imports, commented-out blocks, duplicate data files, or one-off relative imports (`../../`) — use `@/`
- Align naming, quotes, and import order with neighboring files
- Types live in `src/types`; do not redefine the same interface in a component
- Secrets and IDs go in `.env.local` (`VITE_*`), never hardcoded
- Package manager is Yarn: `yarn`, `yarn dev`, `yarn build`

```ts
// ❌ BAD
const WHATSAPP = "https://wa.me/916380799589"; // buried in Contact.tsx

// ✅ GOOD
import { BRAND } from "@/config/brand";
<a href={BRAND.whatsapp}>WhatsApp</a>
```
